{{quotation|game|A record of your many deeds. Carrying this relic causes an extra boss to spawn in [[Perdition Rock]], [[Raisu Palace]], [[the Ruptured Heart]], or [[Sacnoth Valley]].  {{gray|This item cannot be [[trade]]d or sold.}}}}

==Effect==
While this item is carried by a [[party]] member, the following bosses will spawn (in addition to existing spawns for their associated zones). These bosses possess unique [[List of PvE-only skills|PvE-only]] [[elite skill]]s that can only be [[capture]]d from them this way: 
*[[Abaddon's Cursed]] in [[Perdition Rock]]
** {{n}} {{skill icon|Soul Taker}}
** {{e}} {{skill icon|Over the Limit}}
*[[Blade Ancient Syu-Shai]] in [[Raisu Palace (explorable area)]]
** {{w}} {{skill icon|Seven Weapons Stance}}
** {{a}} {{skill icon|Shadow Theft}}
** {{rt}} {{skill icon|Weapons of Three Forges}}
*[[Fureyst Sharpsight]] in [[Sacnoth Valley]]
** {{r}} {{skill icon|"Together as One!"}}
** {{me}} {{skill icon|Time Ward}}
*[[Yoannh the Rebuilder]] in [[The Ruptured Heart]]
** {{mo}} {{skill icon|Judgment Strike}}
** {{p}} {{skill icon|Heroic Refrain}}
** {{d}} {{skill icon|Vow of Revolution}}

==Acquisition==
* One in exchange for 5 [[Proof of Legend|Proofs of Legend]] with the [[Ancient Anniversary Weaponsmith]].

== Notes ==
* The Proof of Triumph is not "consumed" by capturing any of these skills and will remain in the inventory.
* The elite skills count toward all three [[skill hunter]] titles.

== Trivia ==
* These are the only PvE-only Elite skills that are linked to a profession's [[attribute]].
* Until the addition of [[Soul Ignition]], these were also the only PvE-only skills that were linked to a profession's [[attribute]].

